<newsitem itemid="515575" id="root" date="1997-04-16" xml:lang="en">
<title>ITALY: Italy February producer prices rose 0.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Italy February producer prices rose 0.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics office ISTAT gave the following Italian producer price data for February.</p>
<p>    PRODUCER PRICES	   Feb 97    Jan 97	 Feb 96</p>
<p>    Year/year change	  +0.8 pct  +0.9 pct     +4.9 pct</p>
<p>    Month/month change	 0.0 pct  +0.3 pct	0.2 pct</p>
<p>    Index (base 1995=100)   102.6	102.6	  101.8</p>
<p>Istat gave the following general breakdown:</p>
<p>				  Mo/Mo change (%)    Yr/Yr change (%)</p>
<p>    Consumer goods	   0.0 pct		   +0.6 pct</p>
<p>    Investment goods	+0.1 pct		   +2.1 pct</p>
<p>    Intermediate goods    -0.1 pct		   +0.8 pct</p>
<p>It gave the following sector-by-sector breakdown:</p>
<p>    Sector			    mo/mo (%)	     yr/yr (%)</p>
<p>    Energy products		 -0.6 pct		+6.0 pct</p>
<p>    Minerals and metals	   +0.7 pct		+8.6 pct</p>
<p>    Non-metal minerals	    +0.3 pct		+2.7 pct</p>
<p>    Chemicals			 +0.7 pct		+1.2 pct</p>
<p>    Metal works		     -0.1 pct		-2.4 pct</p>
<p>    Transport vehicles	    -0.1 pct		+1.7 pct</p>
<p>    Food, drink and tobacco     -0.3 pct		-1.2 pct</p>
<p>    Clothing and textiles	 +0.5 pct		+0.1 pct</p>
<p>    Other goods		     +0.1 pct		+1.5 pct</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
